.TH WM-EXPORT-IMPORT 1
.SH NAME
wmexport, wmimport, rioimport \- export or import a window-manager display over Styx
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B wmexport
.br
.B wmimport
.RB [ -d
.IR /dev ]
.RB [ -w
.IR /mnt/wm ]
.I cmd
.RI [ arg ...]
.br
.B rioimport
.I cmd
.RI [ arg ...]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.TP
.B wmexport
Serves the local window manager as a synthetic Styx filesystem
(wmctl, keyboard, pointer, and window-name files under a per-window
.BR clone / N
tree) that a remote or local
.B wmimport
can mount and drive.
.TP
.B wmimport
Mounts a
.B wmexport
filesystem (default
.IR /dev ,
.IR /mnt/wm )
and runs
.I cmd
.RI [ arg ...]
against the Draw context it provides.
.TP
.B rioimport
The Plan 9
.B rio
counterpart: proxies a running
.B rio
window as an Inferno Draw context and runs
.I cmd
.RI [ arg ...]
inside it, rather than mounting an Inferno-native
.B wmexport
service.
.SH SOURCE
.B /appl/cmd/wmexport.b
.br
.B /appl/cmd/wmimport.b
.br
.B /appl/cmd/rioimport.b
